"One gamma line does not give one peak. The photopeak (all the energy absorbed) sits above a Compton continuum ending at the Compton edge, 2E²/(mₑc² + 2E), and photons scattered back from behind the source make a backscatter peak near E/({#} + 2E/mₑc²): {#} and {#} keV for {#} keV.",
"The spectrometer measures pulse height, not energy. The HV and amplifier gain set channels per keV; a fit E = a + b·ch through known lines turns channels into energy. Change the HV or gain and the calibration is gone.",
