"<strong>\"Every peak is a gamma ray from the source.\"</strong> The Compton edge, backscatter peak, lead and iodine X-rays, escape peaks and sum peaks all come from the detector and its surroundings. Only photopeaks mark source lines.",
"<strong>\"Turning up the HV gives more counts.\"</strong> It makes each pulse bigger, so the spectrum moves to higher channels. The photopeak area stays the same as long as the peak stays on scale.",
